WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.313
Editing video in a browser tab with WebAssembly.

2
00:00:05.813 --> 00:00:11.281
How ffmpeg runs inside your browser, why the first run downloads an engine,

3
00:00:11.281 --> 00:00:14.197
and how to get the best speed out of it.

4
00:00:15.597 --> 00:00:18.170
ffmpeg, compiled for the browser.

5
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:23.706
ffmpeg is the open-source tool behind a huge share of the world's video

6
00:00:23.706 --> 00:00:24.408
software.

7
00:00:25.708 --> 00:00:31.233
Why the first run is slower. The ffmpeg engine is about 30 MB.

8
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:36.544
Check your browser. Speed depends on a few browser features.

9
00:00:37.844 --> 00:00:43.081
Where it falls short. Very long 4K videos are still better handled by a

10
00:00:43.081 --> 00:00:43.967
desktop app.

11
00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:48.301
To try it, open Video Trimmer in OpenFile.

12
00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:52.419
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

13
00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:56.104
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

14
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:02.655
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
